slug: nomodel-real-distribution
what: NoModel.probabilityOf fabricates the losing classes. With the
  distribution unavailable it called Probe.score once per class and
  gave EVERY non-winner the same share, (1 - p(best)) / (n - 1) --
  exact for two classes, fiction for three or more. That makes the
  Verdict.ranked added by intent-consumer-seams-a arbitrary below rank
  1, runnerUp a coin flip among ties, and lets a pattern cue promote
  the class the probe ranked LAST past the one it ranked second. Both
  stated uses of ranked (show a person the choice it could not make,
  rank on uncertainty for active learning) read exactly the fabricated
  part. Probe.ranked (2052e5a3) is the seam it lacked; blend reads it
  in one pass instead of n calls.
touches: okay-agent/src/main/scala/okay/agent/NoModel.scala,
  okay-agent/src/test/scala/okay/agent/...
